dogecoin.text:
@Alfredorealp @mcuban At first I was thinking like you : damn this shit will worth nothing because there is potential infinity for it.
But if people use them and keep them and population and economy grow, it's actually fine.
Plus some dogecoin can be lost, that's life. Cash gets lost or destroyed too.

@Alfredorealp @mcuban gold is inflationary too. Humanity has a certain amount of gold, plus some gold adding up by mining each year. 
The new gold comes in small amounts so that doesn't break the price of gold.
Dogecoin seems to be the same : the new dogecoins come in limited quantity.
